## Ignore Visual Studio temporary files, build results, and user settings
.vs/
[Dd]ebug/
[Dd]ebugPublic/
[Rr]elease/
[Re]leasePublic/
x64/
x86/
build/
bin/
obj/

## Ignore published output (we can keep this ignored if we build via CI/CD, or track a separate branch)
publish/

## Ignore system-specific files
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini

## Ignore user-specific files
*.suo
*.user
*.userosscache
*.sln.docstates

## Ignore rider/resharper/omnisharp
.idea/
.rider/
.recommenders/
.omnisharp/

## Ignore compiled files
*.dll
*.exe
*.pdb
*.config
*.log
!web.config # Keep web.config since it is needed for IIS deployment

## Ignore sensitive configuration files (never commit real database passwords)
# appsettings.json
# appsettings.Development.json
# Note: Keep appsettings.json in template format, but don't commit production passwords.
